  "title": "Kabir",
  "summary": "Kabir was a fifteenth-century weaver-poet and mystic revered by both Hindus and Muslims. Encyclopedia.com says the only certain fact about him is that he was born a low-caste Muslim weaver in or near Banaras toward mid-century. The V&A and EBSCO give his dates as 1440 to 1518; EBSCO places him in the Sant strand of bhakti and notes that some scholars see his influence on Guru Nanak.",
